177, "tokens_after": 55177, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_18", "tool": "temporal_reachability", "args": {"source": 1468, "target": 1517, "window": [28025, 66424], "max_wait": 600}, "result_digest": "9d7ad076ffe048d4", "result_summary": "{\"max_wait\": 600, \"n_nodes_reached\": 12, \"reached\": false, \"source\": 1468, \"target\": 1517, \"window\": [28025, 66424]}", "latency_ms": 8, "tokens_before": 55177, "tokens_after": 55177, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_19", "tool": "temporal_reachability", "args": {"source": 695, "target": 1517, "window": [28025, 66424]}, "result_digest": "ff00ae1ed85adb3e", "result_summary": "{\"max_wait\": null, \"n_nodes_reached\": 588, \"reached\": false, \"source\": 695, \"target\": 1517, \"window\": [28025, 66424]}", "latency_ms": 6, "tokens_before": 55177, "tokens_after": 55177, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_30df0d06", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [695, 1495, 1468, 1517], "window": [28025, 66424], "confidence": 0.9, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_18", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_19", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_17", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "No time-respecting chain carries influence from 695 to 1495 in [28025, 66424]. The 600-unit-lag search returns nothing (only 2 nodes reached), and relaxing the lag to infinity still fails, so the obstruction is the temporal ordering itself rather than the 600-unit inter-event budget. Bottlenecks are explicit: 695's sole outgoing contact is 1468 and 1495's sole incoming contact is 1517, yet 1468 cannot reach 1517 within the lag and 695 cannot reach 1517 at all. Alternative explanations were tested and rejected: the two nodes ARE connected when time is ignored (shared 2-hop hubs 274/933) and the reverse route 1495 -> 695 is temporally feasible, showing static connectivity is real but flows the wrong way in time; and the window is densely sampled (7,526 events, 1,954 active nodes) with both neighbourhoods active throughout, so the null result is not an artifact of low volume. Conclusion: cascade absent."}, "raw_final_response": "All evidence gathered. Key findings:\n\n- **No time-respecting path** from 695 \u2192 1495 under the 600-unit constraint (step_03), and none even with *unbounded* waiting (step_04, step_09) \u2014 so the failure is structural/directional in time, not merely a gap-length issue.\n- **Static connectivity does exist** when time is ignored: 695's 2-hop neighbourhood (step_05) and 1495's 2-hop neighbourhood (step_07) share hubs 274/933, and the reverse direction 1495 \u2192 695 *is* temporally reachable (step_13) \u2014 confirming the pair is embedded in one weakly-connected component and that the ordering, not the topology, is what blocks the cascade.\n- Both endpoints are low-degree (5 and 4 events, step_02, step_08); 695's only out-contact is 1468 (step_15) and 1495's only in-contact is 1517 (step_16), and 1468 cannot reach 1517 within the 600-unit lag (step_18); 695 cannot reach 1517 at all (step_19).\n- Volume/popularity confounds controlled: 7,526 events over 1,954 active nodes (step_01) and steady activity in both neighbourhoods across the window (step_10, step_11, step_12, step_17) mean the negative result is not from sparse or misaligned sampling.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_30df0d06\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [695, 1495, 1468, 1517],\n  \"window\": [28025, 66424],\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting chain carries influence from 695 to 1495 in [28025, 66424]. The 600-unit-lag search returns nothing (only 2 nodes reached), and relaxing the lag to infinity still fails, so the obstruction is the temporal ordering itself rather than the 600-unit inter-event budget. Bottlenecks are explicit: 695's sole outgoing contact is 1468 and 1495's sole incoming contact is 1517, yet 1468 cannot reach 1517 within the lag and 695 cannot reach 1517 at all. Alternative explanations were tested and rejected: the two nodes ARE connected when time is ignored (shared 2-hop hubs 274/933) and the reverse route 1495 -> 695 is temporally feasible, showing static connectivity is real but flows the wrong way in time; and the window is densely sampled (7,526 events, 1,954 active nodes) with both neighbourhoods active throughout, so the null result is not an artifact of low volume. Conclusion: cascade absent.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 66590, "total_output_tokens": 4594, "total_tokens": 71184, "total_latency_ms": 68293, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}